executionContract.intendedBehavior:
The host obtains the pinned official Node.js 24 Linux tarball, for x64 and arm64, as the check VM's toolchain.

scripts/local-runner/toolchain.json pins each arch's fixed nodejs.org https .tar.xz URL, sha256 and size. Both arches carry one version, whose major equals CI's node-version.

toolchain-cache.mjs fetchNodeToolchain({arch, cacheDir}) resolves a frozen {file, sha256, size, version} for <cacheDir>/<sha256>.tar.xz. The tarball is kept whole. It is fetched through agent-cache.mjs's newly exported fetchPinnedFile.

fetchPinnedFile is the one shared download-and-verify core:
- manual https-only redirects, at most 5;
- a size bound;
- an exclusive, synced 0600 .part;
- digest verification (sha256 or sha512) before an atomic rename;
- re-verification of a cache hit on one no-follow descriptor;
- cleanup on every failure.

Its codes are neutral PINNED_* ones. fetchAgentBinary maps them to its unchanged AGENT_BINARY_* codes, and fetchNodeToolchain maps them to TOOLCHAIN_*. Tests never touch the network.

sourceAssumptions:
agent-cache.mjs as landed in baa52df (CQ-R10d2):
- refuse(code, fallback) maps unknown codes to AGENT_BINARY_DOWNLOAD_FAILED;
- holdsPin(file, {sha256, size}) opens O_NOFOLLOW and returns a boolean;
- cached(target, binary) lstats, refuses non-files with AGENT_BINARY_INPUT_INVALID, and unlinks a corrupt entry;
- respond(url, fetch) follows at most 5 manual https redirects under AbortSignal.timeout(DOWNLOAD_TIMEOUT_MS);
- download(pin, binary, cacheDir, target, fetch) writes `.${sha256}.${nonce}.part` files and untars the codex member.
